{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/358863-solar-exalted-and-enlightenment-charms-2e","id":358863,"title":"Solar Exalted and Enlightenment Charms (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-04T00:18:11-08:00","id":358863,"title":"Solar Exalted and Enlightenment Charms (2E)","content":"I have a sneaking suspicion this is one of those &quot;gonna feel like a huge idiot once I get the answer&quot; questions, but I'm not certain of the answer, so I'll pose it to you fine folks.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Exalted require the various Enlightenment charms to be able to learn Celestial Martial Arts, and the DB book establishes what prerequisite stats an instructor would require (MA 5, E4 to teach the charms, MA 5 E6 to invent new ones), but what I'm trying to figure out is whether or not those charms are purchasable as general Martial Arts charms for other Exalt types (Solars in this particular situation). I dug through Scroll of the Monk, MoEP<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />B, and skimmed the Errata and Ink Monkeys to try to see if I could find Solar charms for it, but to no avail. Am I just looking in the wrong place, or can they learn those enlightenment charms as a regular MA charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T00:22:37-08:00","id":358884,"title":"","content":"They certainly can, but if you grab Occult 2 you can get better ones from your native charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T01:58:01-08:00","id":358928,"title":"","content":"I'm sure I remember somewhere seeing that they are Celestial Martial Arts charms and so, in theory, a Celestial could buy them, but I can't remember where I saw that. Somewhere extremely obscure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T02:40:18-08:00","id":358942,"title":"","content":"They are. They're not DB-native Charms and they were invented by Celestials ergo Celestials can learn them. <br /> <br /> But yeah they're generally inferior to your native Charms. The big bonus they give is that you can teach them to DB lieutenants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T03:24:27-08:00","id":358993,"title":"","content":"Drowning In Understanding Kata in Lords of Creation specifically says that anyone capable of learning CMAs can learn it, and it has the Tiger And Bear Charms as a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> Also, Dragon Kings <i>have </i>to learn the initiation Charms to learn CMAs, so they are certainly not Terrestrial native.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 01-04-2015, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T17:32:01-08:00","id":359729,"title":"","content":"Okay, Drowning in Understanding Kata states in it's write-up that it is indeed a Celestial MA charm, and can be learned as such, so seeing as it branches out from Tiger And Bear Awareness/Unity, it's safe to assume the prior charms are as well, though no where in MoEP<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />B does it actually specify such.<br /> <br /> I'm curious about these &quot;Occult 2&quot; methods that DrLoveMonkey mentioned. I can't find anything like that in the Occult charms for Solars, anyone know what he's talking about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T17:47:34-08:00","id":359745,"title":"","content":"I assume he means Spirit-Detecting Glance and Spirit-Cutting Attack, which are rather better than Pasiap's Humility and Moment of Danaa'd. I don't think the Tiger-And-Bear pair of Charms have as obvious an analogue in the Solar set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Solar Kitten","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3907-aretii","name":"Aretii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T17:51:32-08:00","id":359750,"title":"","content":"Ahh, so he just misunderstood the question. I'm not looking for &quot;I see spirits/dead things&quot;, I'm looking for &quot;I'm a Solar Exalted instructing a Terrestrial Exalted in the ways of Celestial Martial Arts&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T17:59:08-08:00","id":359759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/358863-solar-exalted-and-enlightenment-charms-2e?p=359729#post359729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about these &quot;Occult 2&quot; methods that DrLoveMonkey mentioned. I can't find anything like that in the Occult charms for Solars, anyone know what he's talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>The function of most of the sets of Enlightenment charms are to observe spirits in their natural habitat, and then allow you to interact with the immaterial. These are both fairly straight forward Solar Occult Charms.<br /> <br /> The Tiger and Bear initiation is a bit unusual in the sense that it basically ignores what everyone else is doing and goes it's own way, but even so I'm not sure you'd really both. Tiger and Bear Awareness is an expensive, difficult to access version of Surprise Anticipation Method and Tiger and Bear Unity is an expensive, Essence 3 version of the Second Excellency. If weren't actually after their enlightening function, or focused on some sort of 'MA is the only ability I'll ever need' shenanigans I'm not sure why you'd bother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1849-suddenthunder","name":"SuddenThunder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1849_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T18:14:43-08:00","id":359788,"title":"","content":"Tiger and Bear Unity is a cap-breaker, so you can use it for mad shenanigans. Its cost is the only real issue it has. I suspect that in actual play it behaves more or less like an expensive DV-halver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T18:21:03-08:00","id":359792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SuddenThunder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/358863-solar-exalted-and-enlightenment-charms-2e?p=359759#post359759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The function of most of the sets of Enlightenment charms are to observe spirits in their natural habitat, and then allow you to interact with the immaterial. These are both fairly straight forward Solar Occult Charms.<br /> <br /> The Tiger and Bear initiation is a bit unusual in the sense that it basically ignores what everyone else is doing and goes it's own way, but even so I'm not sure you'd really both. Tiger and Bear Awareness is an expensive, difficult to access version of Surprise Anticipation Method and Tiger and Bear Unity is an expensive, Essence 3 version of the Second Excellency. If weren't actually after their enlightening function, or focused on some sort of 'MA is the only ability I'll ever need' shenanigans I'm not sure why you'd bother.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The character in question is a Solar Martial Artist that will be taking on a Dragon Blooded student that intends to impart him with the wisdom of Celestrial Martial Arts (eventually.) As far as I'm able to find anywhere, for a Dragon Blooded to even be able to learn CMA, they need to be taught the Enlightenment charms, and to teach the Enlightenment Charms you first have to HAVE the enlightenment charms. Unless I am completely misreading things. In which case, please, point me in the right direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T01:07:40-08:00","id":359999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/358863-solar-exalted-and-enlightenment-charms-2e?p=359792#post359792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character in question is a Solar Martial Artist that will be taking on a Dragon Blooded student that intends to impart him with the wisdom of Celestrial Martial Arts (eventually.) As far as I'm able to find anywhere, for a Dragon Blooded to even be able to learn CMA, they need to be taught the Enlightenment charms, and to teach the Enlightenment Charms you first have to HAVE the enlightenment charms. Unless I am completely misreading things. In which case, please, point me in the right direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct. Or they could theoretically learn those Charms from a manual or tome or something.<br /> <br /> There are 3 written pairs of enlightening Charms. Each is generally from a different historical era. It doesn't matter what pair you teach them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T18:37:56-08:00","id":360815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/358863-solar-exalted-and-enlightenment-charms-2e?p=359999#post359999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are correct. Or they could theoretically learn those Charms from a manual or tome or something.<br /> <br /> There are 3 written pairs of enlightening Charms. Each is generally from a different historical era. It doesn't matter what pair you teach them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha! At last!<br /> <br /> That's what I thought, which is why I was asking of those charms counted as Celestial charms for the purpose of purchasing them as a non-DB, or if there was an existing Solar equivalent somewhere else I hadn't found yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T18:52:24-08:00","id":360822,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Here's a couple I wrote up a while ago, derived from carvings on ancient Dragon King ruins. I have also recently used the first and last Charms of Path of the Arbiter, Meditation on the Enemy and Meditation on Judgement, as a suitable custom Enlightenment pair.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">DRAGON HAS MANY TAILS</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost</b>: 1m; <b>Mins</b>: Martial Arts 3, Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type</b>: Reflexive (Step 5)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Keywords</b>: Combo-OK, Stackable, Enlightening</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Duration</b>: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisite</b> <b>Charms</b>: None</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">This Charm negates a single point of penalty that applies to MPDV and Martial Arts derived PDV. Multiple activations of this charm can be stacked to cancel up to (Martial Arts) points of penalty. </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\">DRAGON BASKS IN THE SUN</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Cost</b>: 3m; <b>Mins</b>: Martial Arts 4, Essence 3</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Type</b>: Reflexive (Step 7)</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Keywords</b>: Combo-OK, Holy, Enlightening</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Duration</b>: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Prerequisite</b> <b>Charms</b>: Dragon Has Many Tails</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\">This Charm reduces the final damage of an attack against the martial artist by 1. Against attacks from Creatures of Darkness, it instead reduces final damage by (Essence/2). Damage cannot be reduced below one die.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T07:46:22-08:00","id":362418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/358863-solar-exalted-and-enlightenment-charms-2e?p=360815#post360815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I thought, which is why I was asking of those charms counted as Celestial charms for the purpose of purchasing them as a non-DB, or if there was an existing Solar equivalent somewhere else I hadn't found yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would hazard a guess that if you have to put a label on them, they'd be called &quot;general MA Charms not affiliated with a Style,&quot; sort of like Master's Hand Envisioned Anew.<br /> <br /> AFAIK there is nothing in the native Solar Charmset that comes close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}